# Competency question (native gmeow:reasoningLogic lane, #1294): "Does the determinant
# preservation law det(A·B) = det(A)·det(B), evaluated as a real logic:Formula, ENTAIL the
# product tuple over concrete determinants?"  matMul(A,B,AB) is a fixed-arity n-ary body atom
# (reified) and mul(dA,dB,dAB) is an n-ary HEAD atom: firing the law DERIVES a content-
# addressed reified tuple logic:instanceOf(R, exa:mulRel) ∧ logic:naryArg{i}(R, ·) — the
# head-derivation path of #1294. No fact asserts this tuple; only the law derives it. Over
# the closure the answer is exactly {dA=detWdA, dB=detWdB, dAB=detWdAB}.
PREFIX exa:   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/algebra/>
PREFIX logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/>

SELECT ?dA ?dB ?dAB WHERE {
    ?r logic:instanceOf exa:mulRel ;
       logic:naryArg0 ?dA ;
       logic:naryArg1 ?dB ;
       logic:naryArg2 ?dAB .
}
